# Copy to frontend/.env.local and fill in.
# Never commit the filled-in file.
#
# There is only one .env here. CopilotKit's built-in agent runs inside the
# Next.js process, so there is no separate agent server to configure.

# ── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Model provider key. Read server-side by BuiltInAgent; never exposed to the
# browser. The built-in agent falls back to this env var automatically for any
# `openai:*` model, so no agent passes `apiKey` explicitly.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# One model id for every agent. The doc pages this repo implements name four
# different ids between them (openai:gpt-5.4-mini, openai:gpt-4.1,
# openai/gpt-4o-mini, and gpt-4o via the AI SDK), so all agents read this.
# Defaults to openai:gpt-4.1 — the only one of the four that appears in the
# Model Selection page's list of supported OpenAI models.
# Both `provider:model` and `provider/model` parse.
# OPENAI_MODEL=openai:gpt-4.1

# ── CopilotKit Intelligence ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# THREE separate credentials, and they gate different things. Two server-side,
# below; the third is NEXT_PUBLIC_COPILOTKIT_LICENSE_KEY at the bottom of this
# file, which is browser-visible and interchangeable with neither.
#
# CPK_INTELLIGENCE_API_KEY is the project API key. It authorizes the runtime
# against the platform: it is what makes /api/copilotkit/info report mode
# "intelligence" and what makes the thread endpoints return real, persisted
# rows. Server-side only — never NEXT_PUBLIC_, or it ships in the browser
# bundle.
#
# Renamed upstream on 2026-09-04: this was INTELLIGENCE_API_KEY, and the docs
# called it a "license key". Both the name and the cpk- prefix changed, so an
# .env carried over from before that date sets a variable the runtime no longer
# reads — it will start in SSE mode with no error.
#
# COPILOTKIT_LICENSE_TOKEN builds the runtime's licenseChecker, which is what
# /info reports as licenseStatus. <CopilotThreadsDrawer> gates its locked
# "Upgrade" view on THAT field, not on the key above — so a runtime can serve
# threads perfectly and still render every drawer locked.
#
# Headless Threads added a paragraph on 2026-09-04: a managed project is never
# issued this token. It covers offline and self-hosted licensing only and does
# not replace the project key above. So on a managed project there is nothing
# to put here, and the drawer's locked view is the expected steady state — see
# README §9.17. Set it only if CopilotKit Engineering issued you one.
#
# Both are optional. Without them the runtime falls back to SSE mode with an
# in-memory runner: chat works on every route, the Rich Threads routes stop
# persisting, and nothing survives a restart. The home page's Connection panel
# reports which mode you are actually in.

# CPK_INTELLIGENCE_API_KEY=cpk-...
# COPILOTKIT_LICENSE_TOKEN=...

# Non-secret analytics identity. Read by CopilotRuntime's constructor, which
# falls back to it when no telemetryId is passed in options. Written to .env by
# the CLI's `init`/`create`, alongside the platform URLs and the project key.
# CPK_TELEMETRY_ID=

# Also listed by Headless Threads as something the CLI writes. No installed
# @copilotkit package reads it — see README §9.18 before setting it.
# SL_ENABLED=

# The identity the provider sends as x-user-id / x-user-name, which the
# runtime's identifyUser callback reads. Threads are per-user, so changing this
# gives you a different thread list — useful for watching them diverge.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_USER_ID=harness-local
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_USER_NAME=Harness User

# ── The other two providers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The /model-selection route runs three agents side by side — Agent A on
# OpenAI, Agent B on Google, Agent C on Anthropic — each reading its own key.
# A column whose key is missing says so instead of offering a chat, so these
# are optional: set them only for the providers you want to exercise.
#
# No extra packages are needed. @ai-sdk/anthropic and @ai-sdk/google ship as
# dependencies of @copilotkit/runtime, and the runtime picks the provider from
# the model prefix.

# GOOGLE_API_KEY=...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Per-provider model ids for those three agents. Defaults come from the Model
# Selection page's own tables of supported models.
# OPENAI_MODEL also sets the id for every other agent in the app (above).
# GOOGLE_MODEL=google:gemini-2.5-flash
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-5
#
# Note the HYPHENS in the Anthropic id. The CopilotKit docs print dotted
# versions ("claude-sonnet-4.5") but Anthropic's API only knows the hyphenated
# form and 404s on the other. OpenAI and Google keep their dots.

# The third credential: a publishable, browser-visible key, passed to the
# provider as publicLicenseKey. The Inspector page is explicit that it is NOT
# the same thing as the server-side CPK_INTELLIGENCE_API_KEY that `copilotkit
# project select` writes, and that neither substitutes for the other. The
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix is correct here and would be a leak on either of the two
# server-side keys above.
#
# No route in this repo needs it.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_COPILOTKIT_LICENSE_KEY=ck_pub_...
